description:
Find launches from a date window that Product Hunt's proprietary model ranks as likely to raise a Series A within two years of launch.
Use it to surface promising startups; it is not investment advice.

When to use: "promising startups that launched last month", "which recent launches look fundable", "the strongest new YC startups",
or any request to shortlist new startups by potential. For a plain, unranked list of recent launches, use search_products instead.

Only launches in the model's Top 10% are returned, strongest first. series_a_band ranks the launch against all Product Hunt launches, from "Top 0.1%" to
"Top 10%". Quote it as given ("Product Hunt's model ranks this launch in the Top 1%"); it is a ranking, not a probability.

Results are paged: when next_cursor is present, call again with the same arguments plus cursor to get the next page.
Scores settle over a launch's first two days. For a daily run, look back three days and skip launches already seen.

For example:
  "which recent launches look fundable?" → {}
  "promising consumer AI startups" → { "query": "consumer ai" }
  "AI agent startups from Q3 2026 likely to raise" → { "category_slug": "ai-agents", "launched_after": "2026-07-01", "launched_before": "2026-09-30" }
  "which recent YC launches look strongest?" → { "yc_only": true }

Find software, apps, AI tools, developer tools and MCP servers by need, name or launch date.
Each result is a product with up to 3 launches.

Use it to look up a product by name, find tools for a need, or browse by category and date.
To find MCP servers set has_mcp_server, or use search_mcp_servers to weigh the user's current tools.
For a leaderboard use get_product_leaderboard; for alternatives to one product use get_alternatives;
for reviews and full details use get_product_profile.

Omit filters and sort the user did not ask for. Put constraints in their own fields, not in query. Examples:
- "is Raindrop on Product Hunt?" → {"query": "raindrop"}
- "free open source screen recorders" → {"query": "screen recorder", "pricing": "free", "open_source": true}
- "MCP servers for project management" → {"query": "project management", "has_mcp_server": true}
- "AI agents with the most points in the last 7 days" → {"category": "ai-agents", "launched_within_days": 7, "sort": "most_points"}
